    {
      "title": "response.ok, Status and Parsing JSON",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "response.ok, Status and Parsing JSON",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Check response.ok",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "fetch ==rejects== only on network failure or abort",
                "HTTP 404/500 still **resolve**",
                "`res.ok` is true for status ==200-299=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const res = await fetch(u);",
                "if (!res.ok) throw new Error(res.status);",
                "const data = await res.json();"
              ],
              "note": "check ok before parsing"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Body Parsers",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Method",
                "Gives"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`res.json()`",
                  "parsed JSON"
                ],
                [
                  "`res.text()`",
                  "string"
                ],
                [
                  "`res.blob()`",
                  "Blob"
                ],
                [
                  "`res.formData()`",
                  "FormData"
                ],
                [
                  "`res.arrayBuffer()`",
                  "ArrayBuffer"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Each parser returns a ==Promise==",
                "Body is read ==once==; `bodyUsed` becomes true",
                "`res.clone()` before a second read"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Empty or Invalid JSON",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`res.json()` rejects on empty or invalid body",
                "204 No Content has no body",
                "Check the status, or read `text()` first"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "A 404 is not an error to fetch: ==check res.ok== every time."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "AbortController and Timeouts",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "AbortController and Timeouts",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Cancel a request",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`ctrl.signal` goes into fetch; ==ctrl.abort()== cancels the request",
                "Aborted fetch rejects with `AbortError`",
                "Ignore the abort names; rethrow real errors"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const ctrl = new AbortController();",
                "fetch(url, { signal: ctrl.signal }).catch(e => {",
                "  if (e.name === 'AbortError' ||",
                "      e.name === 'TimeoutError') return;",
                "  throw e;",
                "});",
                "ctrl.abort();"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Timeout and combine",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Signal",
                "Rejects with"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`ctrl.abort()`",
                  "`AbortError`"
                ],
                [
                  "`AbortSignal.timeout(5000)`",
                  "`TimeoutError` after 5s"
                ],
                [
                  "`AbortSignal.any([a, b])`",
                  "reason of the signal that fired"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Combine user cancel and timeout: ==first to fire== wins"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "signal: AbortSignal.any([",
                "  ctrl.signal, AbortSignal.timeout(5000)",
                "])"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Single-use controller",
              "text": "Once aborted, it stays aborted: ==new controller per request==. In React, call `abort()` in the effect cleanup to drop stale responses."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
